# Variable Naming

- **No shorthands**: Use full, clear names. Prefer a long and clear variable name to a short one.
- **Minimum length**: A variable name should never be less than three characters.

## Examples

- Use `element` instead of `el`
- Use `elementId` instead of `id` (when it denotes an element identifier)
- Use `storedValue` instead of `val`
- Use `ingredientElement` instead of `el` for a looked-up element
- Use `tierA` / `tierB` (or `firstTier` / `secondTier`) instead of `a` / `b` in sort callbacks
- Use `iconUrl` for icon URL parameters/variables
- In list callbacks, use descriptive names: `element`, `recipe`, `referencingElement` rather than `item`, `el`, `id` when the meaning is an element or entity

Property names on existing types (e.g. `element.id`, JSON `"id"`) stay as defined by the API/data model.
